Package: folio-post
Version: 0.5.1
Section: mail
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Installed-Size: 3000
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, librsvg2-common, libsqlite3-0, tzdata
Recommends: gir1.2-secret-1, gnupg, openssl, python3-enchant, hunspell-en-us | hunspell-dictionary, xdg-utils, fonts-crosextra-carlito, pst-utils, libemail-outlook-message-perl, gnome-online-accounts
Maintainer: Ron Shillings <ron.shillings@gmail.com>
Description: ribbon mail program
 Folio Post is a mail program with a ribbon interface, KeyTips, a Folder
 Pane, message list and Reading Pane, and the standard desktop mail
 keyboard shortcuts. It works with Gmail (Google sign-in or an app
 password), Proton Mail through Proton Mail Bridge, and any IMAP, POP3 and
 SMTP account, and calendars from Google, any CalDAV server and internet
 (.ics) links such as Proton Calendar's. Mail is kept on this computer
 and readable offline; pictures from the internet aren't loaded until
 allowed.
